WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.272
First, log in to the FoodRescue Link website or app.

2
00:00:04.512 --> 00:00:09.648
Today, Peddie dining hall has twelve servings of fresh salad to share.

3
00:00:09.888 --> 00:00:14.064
I enter the food name and quantity, then upload a photo.

4
00:00:14.304 --> 00:00:20.904
Next, the pickup location and time. And a quick reminder: bring a reusable bag.

5
00:00:21.144 --> 00:00:28.200
Looks good. Publish! These twelve servings are ready for Rise to receive.

6
00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:39.360
In this demo, Peddie sends twelve servings of salad to Rise. A volunteer receives the donation.

7
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:46.846
Rise has its own food, too. Today, we have six portions of pasta and eight portions of soup.

8
00:00:47.086 --> 00:00:50.230
We also welcome donations from the school.

9
00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:55.894
Here are twelve servings of salad from Peddie. Let me confirm the quantity.

10
00:00:56.134 --> 00:01:02.710
I add our pickup location. Great, residents can now reserve food from either source.

11
00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:07.012
Oh, there is plenty to choose from.

12
00:01:07.252 --> 00:01:15.796
The salad is donated by Peddie. The pasta and soup are supplied by Rise. Each source is clearly labeled.

13
00:01:16.036 --> 00:01:20.548
There is fruit, bread, and ingredients I can cook at home, too.

14
00:01:20.788 --> 00:01:24.124
Today, I will take two portions of pasta.

15
00:01:24.364 --> 00:01:29.524
Reserved! I just need to show this pickup code when I arrive.

16
00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:40.680
The neighbor goes to Rise with a pickup code. A volunteer checks the reservation and hands over the food.

17
00:01:40.874 --> 00:01:44.642
Hi there! May I see your pickup code?

18
00:01:44.882 --> 00:01:51.314
Let me check. Yes, that is right. Two portions of pasta.

19
00:01:51.554 --> 00:01:57.050
All confirmed. Here you go. Enjoy your meal!

20
00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:05.000
FoodRescue Link turns food waste into community resilience,
helping donors share responsibly.
